  "source": "Chebfun7574c77 @chebtech2/vals2coeffs.m: generalcomplex IFFT, real/pureimag branches, exact even/odd corrections.",
  "reason": "Split real/imag FFT preserved strict conjugacy but produces cutoff16 on retained33point REAL input, whereas native constructor gives15. Literal generalcomplex IFFT yields15 but violates exactconjugacy by1.9864e-16. Canonical orientation yields15 and preserves conjugacy.",
  "algorithm": "Per-column first nonzero imaginary sample chooses conjugation; canonical pairs share one FFT input. Pureimag columns rotate onto real branch; finite primal real projection uses stop_gradient so transverse complex tangents remain. Undo rotation/conjugation, retain prior source even/odd correction. One IFFT.",
  "source_boundary": "Orientation is explicit numerical backend adaptation based on real DCT matrix conjugacy; MATLAB does not implement this convention. No blanket bitwise native FFT or cutoff parity claim.",
